    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Done. The build succeeds and all tests pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`). The audit output confirms the new format working end-to-end: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27`, HASH8 `16E6609E`, Luhn CHK `1`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Unified identifier** \u2014 `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (no separators):\n- **`common/MemberId.java`** (new, replaces `CustomerCode.java`) \u2014 `base(region, fy, telephone, lastName)` builds `REGION+FY+HASH8` then appends `Luhn.checkDigit` over that core; `regionOf` reads the leading alphabetic run; `fiscalYearLabel` reads the two FY digits after the region.\n- **`owner/AssignOwnerMemberId.java`** (new, replaces `AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 computes the memberId (pulling FY from the owner's already-adjusted `registrationDate`) and applies collision handling to the **memberId** (`-<n>` suffix, n\u22652).\n\n**Field removals**:\n- `Owner` entity: `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; renamed all four DB schemas (widened to `VARCHAR(32)`).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added `memberId`. Kept `fiscalYear` but now derived from the memberId's FY segment.\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped the `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; `fiscalYear`, `locality`, `timezone` now read from `memberId`. `memberId` auto-maps entity\u2192DTO.\n\n**References to memberId** (per the spec):\n- `OwnerSegment` and `Localities.localityOf/timezoneOf` read the region from `memberId`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` logs `memberId` (dropped the `membershipNumber` line); `OwnerCreatedEvent` record field and JSON key are now `memberId`.\n- `owners.POST.yml`: `assignCustomerCode` step \u2192 `assignMemberId`, with updated comments.",
